        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: تعذر",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "تعذر — taʿadhdhara — \"to prove impossible\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "تعذر علينا السفر بسبب الطقس. taʿadhdhara ʿalaynā as-safar bi-sabab aṭ-ṭaqs. Travelling proved impossible for us because of the weather."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Present: يتعذر, yataʿadhdhar."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It takes على for the person: تعذر (taʿadhdhara) عليه …."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "تعذر (taʿadhdhara) is built on the native Arabic root ʿ-dh-r, \"to excuse\" (Lane). It is Form V; Lane gives it for an affair that became hard to bring about, and so impracticable: to prove impossible."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for saying what happens if."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
